Subject: fix(runtime): load the harness environment for dummy behaviour operations

A scripted behaviour operation cannot see the harness environment, so
assert_env reports a correctly delivered variable as unset:

  ! Dummy runtime: assert_env GH_HOST unset or empty:
  ! Agent exited with code 1

The harness environment is not process state in the sandbox. It is a file,
written once during setup from env.sandbox and whatever host_files
contributed, and the real runtimes source it when they launch — buildRunCommand
does it for the Claude runtime, and checkSandboxGitHubConnectivity does it for
the GitHub pre-flight. Behaviour operations go through sandbox.Exec, which
starts a fresh shell per call that inherits nothing from earlier ones, and none
of them sourced that file. So every operation ran with an environment no real
runtime would ever see.

assert_env is where it shows up first, but it is not the only one affected: any
operation needing a credential or a PATH entry from the harness was failing, or
would fail, for a reason unrelated to what it was checking. Load the file for
each operation that runs a command on the scenario's behalf. write_fixture's
mkdir and its upload stay independent, since that plumbing can legitimately run
before the environment matters.

A missing or unreadable file is reported as itself rather than tolerated. If
the harness environment is absent then the scenario is not exercising what it
claims to, and continuing silently would attribute that to the operation.

The environment file path becomes overridable on DummyRuntime, next to ExecFn,
UploadFn and WriteResultsFn, so the existing tests that run generated commands
in a real host shell can point at a file that exists there. Those tests are
about checkout semantics and were previously passing only because nothing
sourced anything.

Diagnosed by reproducing it in a live sandbox: the identical assertion fails
unsourced and passes sourced against a correct environment file, and a
subsequent exec sees nothing the previous one set.

Breadboard note: patches Go source, so it belongs to the build patch list in
deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh rather than the mirror list. Written to
be sent upstream as-is. Add a DCO sign-off before submitting it as a
human-authored change.

